# ============================================================
# Frontend (Vite / React): no environment variables are required.
# ============================================================
# The app calls the API at the relative path /api. In development Vite proxies /api to the backend
# (vite.config.js), and in production Vercel rewrites /api to the Render backend (vercel.json), so the
# browser only ever talks to its own origin and there is no CORS to configure.
#
# Backend settings live in backend/.env (see backend/.env.example), never in this file.